  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x5">
    <title>FFTDMPME - </title>
    <description>FFTDMPME is an FFT-based damping coefficient used in the ME7.2 knock/vibration detection algorithm, applied as a low-pass filter on frequency-domain cylinder pressure signals to suppress false knock triggers from road noise or exhaust resonance. The single MOV_R12_TABLE_LOAD call site at 0x74ECE is consistent with loading a global scalar into the knock-detection ISR context; the dimensionless VAL_BLK type and low ME7.8 shape correlation (r=0.281) are expected for a single-value parameter with no tabular shape to correlate.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1"/>
